Let a build cap the size of the arenas mimalloc reserves

mimalloc doubles the size of the arenas it reserves every eight arenas,
which costs nothing where reserving only maps address space. Where it
takes real memory, as in a WebAssembly memory that never shrinks, the
late arenas are each a large share of the memory for what may be a small
need. MI_ARENA_MAX_RESERVE, when defined, caps that growth; the default
build leaves it undefined and is unchanged.

License: MIT (mimalloc v3.3.2, as libmimalloc-sys 0.1.49 vendors it)

--- a/c_src/mimalloc/v3/src/arena.c
+++ b/c_src/mimalloc/v3/src/arena.c
@@ -328,6 +328,11 @@
     if (!mi_mul_overflow(multiplier, arena_reserve, &reserve)) {
       arena_reserve = reserve;
     }
+    #ifdef MI_ARENA_MAX_RESERVE
+    if (arena_reserve > MI_ARENA_MAX_RESERVE) {
+      arena_reserve = MI_ARENA_MAX_RESERVE;
+    }
+    #endif
   }
 
   // try to accommodate the requested size for huge allocations
